# Memory Index

One line per memory file, newest first. Each memory is one markdown file in
this directory holding a single durable fact (a validated bug workaround, an
alert level the user set, a design decision), with frontmatter:

```markdown
---
name: short-kebab-case-slug
description: one-line summary used to decide relevance during recall
metadata:
  type: user | feedback | project | reference
---

The fact. For feedback/project entries, follow with **Why:** and
**How to apply:** lines. Link related memories with [[their-name]].
```

Example index entries:

- [eToro rates multi-ID quirk](etoro-rates-quirk.md) — batch endpoint is last-wins; fetch per-ID and merge
- [BTC alert level](btc-alert-60k.md) — alert the user if BTC < 60k, set 2026-01-15
